    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1976-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The divisor \\(d\\) divides both \\(358=2\\cdot179\\) and \\(895=5\\cdot179.\\) Their greatest common divisor is \\(179,\\) a prime, so \\(d=179.\\) Since \\(1059=5\\cdot179+164,\\) we have \\(r=164\\) and \\(d-r=15.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "A common remainder means \\(d\\) divides every pairwise difference",
        "Use \\(1417-1059=358=2\\cdot179\\) and \\(2312-1417=895=5\\cdot179\\)"
      ],
